deployed: 2026-05-12T12:00:00Z · v1.0.74 (Two bugs: widget config showed
generic note + Terminal panes stayed on mock HTML.

USER REPORTS:
  "all widget configs show: This is a built-in terminal pane. Behavior
  + refresh cadence are baked in."
  "and in terminal no widget displays are updated"

BUG 1 — Widget gear opens with generic schema
  Cause: _crTermPaneQuickConfig() resolved schemas via
    _CR_PANE_SCHEMAS[w.type]
  but pinned terminal panes carry w.type === 'pane' with the
  specific id on w.paneId / w.sourceId / w.payload. Every
  pane therefore hit the GENERIC fallback at _CR_PANE_SCHEMAS['pane']
  ("built-in terminal pane…"), masking the rich per-pane
  schemas we built in v1.0.60 / v1.0.68 / v1.0.70 / v1.0.71
  (Top Tokens, Trending, Sniper Activity, Wallet Watchlist,
  Coin Watchlist — every one).

  Fix: try 'pane:<paneId>' key FIRST when w.type === 'pane',
  fall back to widget type, fall back to generic.

BUG 2 — Terminal panes stay on mock HTML
  Cause: _forceTickForVisiblePanes only fired on .crTerm-tab
  click events. Opening the Terminal app via keyboard
  shortcut / desktop icon / programmatic call doesn't
  dispatch a tab-click, so panes inside the window stayed
  un-tagged + un-refreshed until the user clicked something.

  Fix: MutationObserver hook on #win-terminal. Watches the
  window's own class/style attribute (open/close transition)
  and its .crTerm-tabs subtree (internal view switch). On
  any visible-state change, re-runs tagPanes() +
  _stampEngineLiveChips() + _forceTickForVisiblePanes() at
  +60ms. Belt-and-suspenders: observer hook installs at
  boot+500ms with a retry at boot+2500ms in case the
  win-terminal element late-mounts.

After this patch, opening Terminal → switching to Solana
should paint live data within ~1s of the window appearing.
If panes still show mock data, the cause is API-key on the
data side (no Birdeye / GoldRush key → solTopTokens,
solHolders, cexWhales etc fail their fetch silently —
header should now visibly say "offline" or "no data").)

