deployed: 2026-05-12T11:00:00Z · v1.0.72 (Force-tick + re-tag on every
Terminal tab click and on Terminal app launch.

USER REPORT: Solana tab still showed all-mock data after v1.0.68-71.

ROOT CAUSE: The master tick fires every 15 seconds. If a user clicked
the Solana tab right after switching from Engine, they'd see the
original static HTML for up to 14 seconds until the next tick caught
them. Also, if the v1.0.60 _boot ran before the Terminal app's first
render, tagPanes wouldn't find some panes and they'd stay un-tagged
until the first user click.

FIX: Every Terminal tab click now (200ms after the click, to let the
view-toggle complete) runs:
  · tagPanes() — re-walk Solana + CEX views, assign data-pane-id to
    any pane that lost it / never got one
  · _stampEngineLiveChips() — paint .live class on Engine tags
  · _forceTickForVisiblePanes() — for every refresher whose pane
    body exists in the DOM, reset its _lastRun + fire it immediately

Same triple-action also runs:
  · 400ms after any click on a Terminal app launcher (data-os-app=
    "terminal" / data-app="terminal") — catches the case of the
    user opening the Terminal app
  · at boot+3s and boot+8s — catches late-attached DOM cases

Result: the moment the user switches to a tab, every pane on it
either paints LIVE data or surfaces an offline / rate-limited /
cors-blocked tag. No more 15-second mock-data window.

If after reload the user STILL sees mock data, the cause is on the
data-source side:
  · No Birdeye API key configured → solTopTokens/solTrending header
    chip shows "offline"
  · No GoldRush API key → solHolders/solSmart/solSniper/phxWhales
    silently return early (no chip change). Fix: paste a free
    GoldRush key in Token Terminal settings.)

